    "title": "Zen: The Reflective Waters",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "template": "Deep within the [adjective_1] gardens, there sits a lake so still it acts as a celestial mirror. The water captures the [celestial_body] with such precision that one cannot tell sky from earth. Every petal that falls onto the surface sends out ripples of pure silence.\n\nYou approach the edge, feeling your heart beat in a [adverb_1] rhythm. As you gaze down, the reflection does not show your face, but rather a [color] aura of your inner peace. It is a moment where the noise of the world fades into a soft whisper.\n\nSuddenly, a [animal] leaps across the bank, momentarily breaking the liquid glass. You do not flinch, for you understand that [gerund] is merely a part of the grand design. The water begins to [verb_1] once more, settling into a state of perfect clarity.\n\nWithin this clarity, you see the [object_1] you have been searching for all your life. It glows with a soft light, promising that everything is exactly as it should be. You realize that the mirror is not outside, but [preposition] your own spirit.\n\nLeaving the garden, you carry the [feeling] of the water within your chest. The path ahead seems bright and welcoming under the soft glow of twilight. You are the mirror, and the world is simply your reflection.",
